  "description": "PIVVAV crystallizes in the rhombohedral crystal system with space group R -3. Reported CIF formula moiety: C24 H50 Ce6 Cl8 N48 O6,6.67(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 3 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.796-3.801 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 115.39-118.91°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Ce6(μ3-O)4(μ3-OH)2(μ3-Cl)2Cl6(μ2-4-NH2-1,2,4-Triaz)12]·7H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
